# Interactive cursors

Tailwind Preflight sets `cursor: default` on `<button>`. Without an explicit cursor class, buttons and custom click targets often show the arrow instead of a hand — a common polish miss.

## Required classes

| Element | Cursor class |
|---------|----------------|
| `<button>`, clickable controls, tabs, icon buttons | `cursor-pointer` |
| `<a href="...">` | `cursor-pointer` (verify; add if missing) |
| `onClick` on non-button elements (`div`, `span`, `li`, cards) | `cursor-pointer` |
| `disabled` or `aria-disabled` controls | `disabled:cursor-not-allowed` (keep `cursor-pointer` on enabled state) |
| `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>` | Do **not** use `cursor-pointer`; default / `cursor-text` is correct |
| Drag handles, resize grips | `cursor-grab` / `active:cursor-grabbing` |
| Loading but still clickable | keep `cursor-pointer`; use `disabled:cursor-not-allowed` when truly disabled |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ Missing cursor — looks inert on hover
<button className="rounded-md bg-accent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-bg">
  Save
</button>

// ✅ Pointer on interactive; not-allowed when disabled
<button
  type="button"
  disabled={busy}
  className="cursor-pointer rounded-md bg-accent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-bg disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50"
>
  {busy ? "Saving…" : "Save"}
</button>

// ❌ Div acting as button without pointer
<div role="button" tabIndex={0} onClick={onSelect} className="rounded px-2 py-1">
  Option
</div>

// ✅
<div
  role="button"
  tabIndex={0}
  onClick={onSelect}
  className="cursor-pointer rounded px-2 py-1 hover:bg-surface-2"
>
  Option
</div>
```

## Checklist when adding or editing UI

1. Every new `<button>` or link styled as a control includes `cursor-pointer`.
2. Disabled states use `disabled:cursor-not-allowed`.
3. Custom click targets are never left at the default arrow cursor.
4. Text fields and the manuscript editor are not given `cursor-pointer`.
